{
"dur": 37.641,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 7.36,
"text": "On the forum he learns about a scam called SIM swapping. Criminals trick a phone company into moving your number to their SIM card.",
"end": 7.635
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 7.635,
"vo_start": 7.91,
"vo_end": 15.791,
"text": "Many accounts send login codes by text. So whoever controls your number can reset your passwords, from email to bank to crypto.",
"end": 16.066
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 16.066,
"vo_start": 16.341,
"vo_end": 28.021,
"text": "In 2019 a Seattle investor, Greg Bennett, lost over 100 Bitcoin this way. The New York Times later linked the attack to Graham's online alias. He was a minor, and was never charged for it.",
"end": 28.296
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 28.296,
"vo_start": 28.571,
"vo_end": 36.691,
"text": "Soon afterwards, Graham is living large: his own apartment, a white BMW, a Rolex covered in gems. He's still 17.",
"end": 37.641
}
],
